 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Big Sal sawed his helicopter's tail propeller off to save forty bucks.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.812
  },
  {
   "text": "Then he loaded it with three hundred pizzas for the mayor's birthday.",
   "s": 4.012,
   "e": 6.884
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Cut the fat!\" he said. Pepper the pigeon, who hates flying, buckled up.",
   "s": 7.084,
   "e": 10.403
  },
  {
   "text": "Gina lifted off. The helicopter went up. Then it went around.",
   "s": 10.603,
   "e": 13.491
  },
  {
   "text": "And around, like a salad spinner full of pepperoni.",
   "s": 13.691,
   "e": 15.784
  },
  {
   "text": "Forty pizzas flew out the door like frisbees, onto the mayor's limo.",
   "s": 15.984,
   "e": 19.526
  },
  {
   "text": "So Sal grabbed the tail and pulled. Now Sal was spinning too.",
   "s": 19.726,
   "e": 22.497
  },
  {
   "text": "How can one tiny propeller stop a whole helicopter from twirling?",
   "s": 22.697,
   "e": 25.776
  },
  {
   "text": "Push the big blades around one way, and they shove the helicopter the other way.",
   "s": 26.076,
   "e": 29.654
  },
  {
   "text": "Spin on an office chair and swing your arms right: the chair turns left.",
   "s": 30.054,
   "e": 33.544
  },
  {
   "text": "So that little tail propeller pushes sideways all day, to cancel the spin.",
   "s": 33.744,
   "e": 37.483
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Cut the fat,\" Sal whispered, dizzy, gluing it back on.",
   "s": 37.683,
   "e": 39.944
  },
  {
   "text": "Pepper flew the last pizza down himself. Forty bucks, plus tip.",
   "s": 40.144,
   "e": 43.331
  }
 ],
